-02 (Ph1/2)", "outcome": "safety, tolerability and preliminary efficacy (no posted results)", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "rct", "ref_id": "NCT05820152"}, {"study_label": "Mito antioxidants AD review (meta)", "outcome": "mitochondrial dynamics", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": false, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "41596136"}, {"study_label": "Mito antioxidants AD review (meta)", "outcome": "cognitive performance", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": false, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "41596136"}, {"study_label": "Mito antioxidants AD review (meta)", "outcome": "dementia-related pathology", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": false, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "41596136"}, {"study_label": "NR/NMN aging multimorbidity meta (meta)", "outcome": "vascular function", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": true, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "42781074"}, {"study_label": "NR/NMN aging multimorbidity meta (meta)", "outcome": "metabolic health", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": true, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "42781074"}, {"study_label": "Mito-targeted strategies aging review (meta)", "outcome": "clinical transformation of mitochondria-targeted therapies", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "42253926"}, {"study_label": "Redox/mito kidney disease review (meta)", "outcome": "progression from AKI to CKD and worsening of DKD (pathogenic role)", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "42650814"}, {"study_label": "Redox/mito kidney disease review (meta)", "outcome": "redox-mediated mitochondrial injury as a therapeutic target", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "42650814"}, {"study_label": "Sodium selenite septic cardiomyopathy (preclin)", "outcome": "cardiac function", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": false, "evidence": "preclinical", "ref_id": "42460027"}, {"study_label": "Sodium selenite septic cardiomyopathy (preclin)", "outcome": "mtROS accumulation", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": false, "evidence": "preclinical", "ref_id": "42460027"}, {"study_label": "Sodium selenite septic cardiomyopathy (preclin)", "outcome": "ferroptosis", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": false, "evidence": "preclinical", "ref_id": "42460027"}, {"study_label": "NR AYA-HCT factorial (Ph2)", "outcome": "muscle strength and functional capacity endpoints (no posted results)", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "rct", "ref_id": "NCT05194397"}], "gap_cells": [{"intervention": "Elamipretide", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 6, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42794697", "42229401", "40816230", "NCT05168774", "NCT07531251", "NCT05162768"]}, {"intervention": "NAD+ precursors (NR/NMN)", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 2, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42489969", "42669151"]}, {"intervention": "Mito therapies pooled (idebenone, taurine, doxribtimine, elamipretide)", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42361626"]}, {"intervention": "PMD emerging therapies (antioxidant/metabolic, gene therapy, nucleoside therapy)", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42630618"]}, {"intervention": "MNV-201 mitochondrial-augmented cell therapy", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["NCT06017869"]}, {"intervention": "Mitochondria-targeted agents pooled (31 studies)", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42440741"]}, {"intervention": "Mito-targeted therapies pooled incl. SGLT2i/ranolazine (arms not separable)", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42495453"]}, {"intervention": "MitoQ", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42479041"]}, {"intervention": "Urolithin A", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 2, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42616901", "42432192"]}, {"intervention": "Luteolin", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42013553"]}, {"intervention": "NMN", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 2, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42573891", "42429864"]}, {"intervention": "Nicotinamide riboside (NR)", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 2, "top_evidence": "rct", "refs": ["NCT05732051", "NCT07563322"]}, {"intervention": "Sodium selenite (selenium supplementation)", "disease": "septic cardiomyopathy", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42460027"]}, {"intervention": "AAV2-ND6 allotopic gene therapy", "disease": "Leber hereditary optic neuropathy", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42709484"]}, {"intervention": "NFS-02 mitochondrial gene therapy", "disease": "Leber hereditary optic neuropathy", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "rct", "refs": ["NCT05820152"]}, {"intervention": "Nicotinamide riboside (NR)", "disease": "AYA HCT survivors", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "rct", "refs": ["NCT05194397"]}, {"intervention": "NR/NMN (NAD+ precursors)", "disease": "age-related multimorbidity", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42781074"]}, {"intervention": "Mito-targeted antioxidants (MitoQ, MitoTEMPO, SS31, SkQ1)", "disease": "Alzheimer's disease", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["41596136"]}, {"intervention": "Mito-targeted strategies (metabolic/kinetic regulation, transplantation, mtDNA base editing)", "disease": "aging-related diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42253926"]}, {"intervention": "Redox/mitochondrial dysfunction strategies", "disease": "acute kidney injury and chronic kidney disease", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42650814"]}], "insights": ["Elamipretide is the only mito-therapy in this set with human efficacy evidence and regulatory approval in primary mitochondrial disease (accelerated approval for Barth syndrome muscle strength; one case report of HF improvement), but cardiac disease modification remains unconfirmed and its Ph2/Ph3/Ph4 trials have no posted results (42794697; 42229401; 40816230; NCT05168774; NCT05162768; NCT07531251).", "In chronic heart failure a 31-study meta-analysis reports significant improvements in LVEF, NYHA class, all-cause mortality and HF hospitalizations for pooled mito-targeted agents, but this is low confidence (heterogeneous agents/trials pooled, surrogate LVEF endpoint, control arms not specifiable), so no GDMT comparator can be verified (42440741).", "No mito-vs-standard-of-care head-to-head comparison exists anywhere in this record set: no record has is_standard_of_care=true or reports a standard-arm effect (idebenone for LHN, GDMT for HF, supportive care for PMD), so every plotted marker is mito-arm only and the SoC contrast is untested; one HF meta pooled mito agents with SGLT2i/ranolazine without separating arms, so it is kept in the gap map but excluded from arm-level plotting (42495453).", "For LHN, preclinical AAV2-ND6 allotopic gene therapy significantly restored visual function and attenuated progression in ND6P25L mice, and NFS-02 (Ph1/2) is ongoing with no posted results; the SoC idebenone itself sits among therapies with negative/inconclusive late-stage outcomes, and a 5,262-person pedigree cohort characterizes penetrance haplogroups but has no therapeutic implication (42709484; NCT05820152; 42361626; 42630618; 42632451).", "NAD+ precursors show a mixed signal: meta-analyses call clinical benefit variable and context-dependent (positive only for vascular/metabolic markers in early human studies), preclinical cardiac benefit in one animal model coexisted with aggravated anemia and impaired heme biosynthesis, and all human HF/HCT trials lack posted results (42489969; 42781074; 42669151; NCT05732051; NCT07563322; NCT05194397).", "Broad preclinical efficacy (MitoQ, urolithin A, luteolin, NMN, sodium selenite) and early cell-therapy (MNV-201) programs have no human efficacy data yet, and reviews identify clinical translation of mito-targeted strategies as the key unmet obstacle (42479041; 42616901; 42432192; 42013553; 42573891; 42429864; 42460027; NCT06017869; 42253926)."]}